„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!Because they believed not in God,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And trusted not in his salvation:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapterN«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.Though he had commanded the clouds from above,¦layout ‚¤text¿And opened the doors of heaven,¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+And had rained down manna upon them to eat,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)And had given them of the corn of heaven.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¹Man did eat angels' food:¦layout ‚¤text¾He sent them meat to the full.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-He caused an east wind to blow in the heaven:¦layout ‚¤textÙ.And by his power he brought in the south wind.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'He rained flesh also upon them as dust,¦layout ‚¤textÙ0And feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.And he let it fall in the midst of their camp,¦layout ‚¤text¾Round about their habitations.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙISo they did eat, and were well filled: For he gave them their own desire;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(They were not estranged from their lust.¦layout ‚¤textÙ-But while their meat was yet in their mouths,¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ>The wrath of God came upon them, and slew the fattest of them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And smote down the chosen men of Israel.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapterN«first_verse ªlast_verse'¦verses˜„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¿For all this they sinned still,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And believed not for his wondrous works.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.Therefore their days did he consume in vanity,¦layout ‚¤text»And their years in trouble.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(When he slew them, then they sought him:¦layout ‚¤textÙ/And they returned and enquired early after God.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,And they remembered that God was their rock,¦layout ‚¤textÙ And the high God their redeemer.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3Nevertheless they did flatter him with their mouth,¦layout ‚¤textÙ*And they lied unto him with their tongues.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'For their heart was not right with him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+Neither were they stedfast in his covenant.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ!But he, being full of compassion,¦layout ‚¤textÙ/Forgave their iniquity, and destroyed them not:¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ*Yea, many a time turned he his anger away,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ"And did not stir up all his wrath.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+For he remembered that they were but flesh;¦layout ‚¤textÙ/A wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse'…¤book§chapterN«first_verse(ªlast_verse*¦verses“„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/How oft did they provoke him in the wilderness,¦layout ‚¤text½And grieve him in the desert!¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&Yea, they turned back and tempted God,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And limited the Holy One of Israel.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text½They remembered not his hand,¦layout ‚¤textÙ2Nor the day when he delivered them from the enemy.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse*…¤book§chapterN«first_verse+ªlast_verse3¦verses™„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&How he had wrought his signs in Egypt,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And his wonders in the field of Zoan:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'And had turned their rivers into blood;¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And their floods, that they could not drink.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ>He sent divers sorts of flies among them, which devoured them;¦layout ‚¤textÙ And frogs, which destroyed them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ1He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And their labour unto the locust.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#He destroyed their vines with hail,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And their sycomore trees with frost.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)He gave up their cattle also to the hail,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And their flocks to hot thunderbolts.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙSHe cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"By sending evil angels among them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ@He made a way to his anger; He spared not their soul from death,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+But gave their life over to the pestilence;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%And smote all the firstborn in Egypt;¦layout ‚¤textÙ6The chief of their strength in the tabernacles of Ham:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse3…¤book§chapterN«first_verse4ªlast_verse7¦verses”„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/But made his own people to go forth like sheep,¦layout ‚¤textÙ/And guided them in the wilderness like a flock.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3And he led them on safely, so that they feared not:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&But the sea overwhelmed their enemies.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary,¦layout ‚¤textÙ:Even to this mountain, which his right hand had purchased.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)He cast out the heathen also before them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ_And divided them an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse7…¤book§chapterN«first_verse8ªlast_verse:¦verses“„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God,¦layout ‚¤text½And kept not his testimonies:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse8„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ;But turned back, and dealt unfaithfully like their fathers:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,They were turned aside like a deceitful bow.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse9„¥verse:¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ6For they provoked him to anger with their high places,¦layout ‚¤textÙ3And moved him to jealousy with their graven images.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse:…¤book§chapterN«first_verse;ªlast_verse@¦verses–„¥verse;¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"When God heard this, he was wroth,¦layout ‚¤text¼And greatly abhorred Israel:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse;„¥verse<¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#The tent which he placed among men;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse<„¥verse=¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*And delivered his strength into captivity,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And his glory into the enemy's hand.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse=„¥verse>¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,He gave his people over also unto the sword;¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And was wroth with his inheritance.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse>„¥verse?¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"The fire consumed their young men;¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And their maidens were not given to marriage.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse?„¥verse@¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ Their priests fell by the sword;¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And their widows made no lamentation.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse@…¤book§chapterN«first_verseAªlast_verseB¦verses’„¥verseA¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)Then the Lord awaked as one out of sleep,¦layout ‚¤textÙ6And like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseA„¥verseB¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-And he smote his enemies in the hinder parts:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$He put them to a perpetual reproach.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseB…¤book§chapterN«first_verseCªlast_verseH¦verses–„¥verseC¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Moreover he refused the tabernacle of Joseph,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And chose not the tribe of Ephraim:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseC„¥verseD¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text½But chose the tribe of Judah,¦layout ‚¤text¾The mount Zion which he loved.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseD„¥verseE¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-And he built his sanctuary like high palaces,¦layout ‚¤textÙ2Like the earth which he hath established for ever.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseE„¥verseF¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ He chose David also his servant,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And took him from the sheepfolds:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseF„¥verseG¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7From following the ewes great with young he brought him¦layout ‚¤textÙ5To feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseG„¥verseH¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart;¦layout ‚¤textÙ0And guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verseH